  "issuedISO": "2026-11-09T08:17:00-10:00",
  "discussion": "A medium period swell out of the north-northwest (340 degree) will hold today as another small to moderate swell fills in later tonight, keeping elevated surf along north and west facing shores through Tuesday. A much larger northwest to north-northwest swell was generated by a gale force low developing east of Kamchatka. This large north-northwest swell may bring warning level surf heights to exposed north and west facing shores building in through the day on Wednesday, peaking Wednesday night, decreasing to advisory levels on Thursday, and then falling below advisory levels by Friday. A small south swell will keep tiny surf in the forecast along south facing shores today before declining through the remainder of the week. Rough surf along east-facing shores will hold at or above seasonal average today. Expect slight decreasing trends as trade winds ease up on Tuesday and Wednesday.",
